~ start
Chancellor Vogel: Herr President. The Chancellery kitchen makes a venison you cannot get in Paris, and I paid for it out of my own pocket, so you may trust the compliment.
- Raise the Rhine shipping tolls => raise_tolls
- Offer a joint grid study => grid_study
~ raise_tolls
Chancellor Vogel: Straight to business over the venison. My inland fleet will scream, but a toll we set together is a toll Bonn cannot be blamed for alone.
- Shake on the joint toll => shake
- Leave it for the officials => officials
~ shake
Chancellor Vogel: Then it is done, and we are both poorer in friends and richer in revenue.
=> END
~ officials
Chancellor Vogel: The officials will bury it, of course. But they will bury it together, which is its own kind of treaty.
=> END
~ grid_study
Chancellor Vogel: A study! The most honest word in European politics: it costs little, commits nothing, and reads well in both parliaments.
- Fund it generously => fund_big
- Fund it modestly => fund_small
~ fund_big
Chancellor Vogel: Generosity, from a French budget? My finance ministry will not believe the cable.
=> END
~ fund_small
Chancellor Vogel: Modest it is. The study will conclude exactly what we paid for it to conclude, as studies do.
=> END
